OTOH, judging from the postings many find these responses enjoyable and 
take part in them.

Myself, I hardly ever see the original post since it's normally been 
spam-killed somewhere in the distribution chain to me, but I like the 
NetHackese responses.
Obviously one shouldn't fall for the reply-to-unrelated-crossposted-
groups trick that they want you to do, but otherwise the behaviour seems 
pretty harmless IMMHO.

I guess if someone does not want to see these he/she could set his/her 
newsreader to not show threads where the original message is cross-
posted or not available (/revoked). 

